{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 2, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 6406056413800506743, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 613, "mtime": 1791871704.7541122, "sha256": "eeca785b7d7c5b072be33ac4cedce9544c4b13be2dd0993765c6f19c085cb703"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 412, "mtime": 1791871708.5383465, "sha256": "6abccdd391f9c7c3727b883290a98c08fb3149654f3c457e2b42ed5f2d879b02"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/transcripts/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/3/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/cells/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/3/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Adding a regression test, then running it:\n`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** there were two problems in `pricing/money.py`:\n1. The float `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999\u2026`, so `round` sees a value just under the halfway point and rounds down.\n2. Python's `round` sends exact halves to the nearest even digit, so `round(0.125, 2)` gives `0.12`. The function's own docstring says it should round halves up.\n\n**Fix:** `round_money` now turns the float into its shortest decimal form (`repr(x)` gives `\"2.675\"`) and rounds that with `Decimal.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP)`. The return type is still `float`, so callers like `add_vat` need no changes.\n\n**Tests:** I added `tests/test_round_money.py`, which checks `2.675\u21922.68`, `1.005\u21921.01`, `0.125\u21920.13` and `-2.675\u2192-2.68`. pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the test functions directly with `python3`. The new tests and the existing `test_split` pass. Plain `round` gives `2.67` and `0.12` for the same inputs, so the new tests would have failed on the old code.\n\n**Separate bug, not fixed:** `split` starts with `int(total * 100)`, which cuts off the fraction instead of rounding. Inputs like `0.29`, stored as `28.999\u2026` cents, give the wrong base amount. I didn't touch it because it's a different bug from the one you asked about.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 7, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 133139, "requests_cache_write": 68539, "requests_cost_usd": 0.41158680000000003, "requests_count": 7, "requests_input_uncached": 16, "requests_output": 2110, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial3", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": nul